TOMER AHARONI: Thank you.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.659
So as you can see, we're
pretty excited by this.

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:40.159
But the question that we must
ask is, where can we go next?

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:42.940
ALON EZER: So we're currently
working with beta testers

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:45.490
to test our service, improve
it, and make it really

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:49.200
something that they can
use every single day.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.150
Besides that, we
have conference calls

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:56.500
that we want to use Nagish
in a more professional way,

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.504
so they can use it
while they work.

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:00.810
TOMER AHARONI: Yeah,
also, we wanted

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.970
to create personalized voices.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:07.380
So for instance, adults won't
have the same voice as child.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.300
We feel like that each person
should have their unique voice,

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:13.650
even if they can't speak.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.480
If you want to hear
